    {
      "id": "qe64c308ee3",
      "text": "A particle moves from point A (2 m, 3 m) to point B (8 m, 11 m). Find the magnitude of its displacement.",
      "owner_label": null,
      "authored": false,
      "subtopic": "Position and displacement in a plane",
      "hint": "Subtract coordinates first.",
      "steps": [
        "Δx = 8 − 2 = 6 m and Δy = 11 − 3 = 8 m.",
        "|Δr| = √(6² + 8²) = 10 m."
      ],
      "answer": "10 m",
      "visual": "<figure data-role=\"visual\"><svg role=\"img\" viewBox=\"0 0 360 240\" aria-labelledby=\"t-b-qe64c308ee3 d-b-qe64c308ee3\"><title id=\"t-b-qe64c308ee3\">Displacement A to B</title><desc id=\"d-b-qe64c308ee3\">Arrow from A to B with components 6 m and 8 m.</desc><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"352\" y2=\"206.0\" stroke=\"#999\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#999\"/><text x=\"338\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12\">x</text><text x=\"40.0\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"12\">y</text><defs><marker id=\"arrow-b-qe64c308ee3\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L9,4.5 L0,9 z\" fill=\"#2c4fb8\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"65.3\" y1=\"159.1\" x2=\"159.1\" y2=\"159.1\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-qe64c308ee3)\"/><text x=\"116.2\" y=\"155.1\" font-size=\"12\">6 m</text><line x1=\"159.1\" y1=\"159.1\" x2=\"159.1\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-qe64c308ee3)\"/><text x=\"163.1\" y=\"92.5\" font-size=\"12\">8 m</text><line x1=\"65.3\" y1=\"159.1\" x2=\"159.1\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-qe64c308ee3)\"/><text x=\"116.2\" y=\"92.5\" font-size=\"12\">Δr</text></svg><figcaption>Displacement A to B</figcaption></figure>",
      "source_identity": null,
      "learner_location": "pages/position-and-displacement-in-a-plane.html#qe64c308ee3"
    },
    {
      "id": "q768643a6ae",
      "text": "A student walks 30 m east and then 40 m north in 50 s. Find the magnitude of the displacement and the average velocity.",
      "owner_label": null,
      "authored": false,
      "subtopic": "Position and displacement in a plane",
      "hint": "The two legs are perpendicular.",
      "steps": [
        "Displacement = √(30² + 40²) = 50 m.",
        "Average velocity = displacement / time = 50 / 50 = 1 m/s, directed about 53° north of east."
      ],
      "answer": "50 m; 1 m/s at about 53° north of east",
      "visual": "<figure data-role=\"visual\"><svg role=\"img\" viewBox=\"0 0 360 240\" aria-labelledby=\"t-b-q768643a6ae d-b-q768643a6ae\"><title id=\"t-b-q768643a6ae\">Walk east then north</title><desc id=\"d-b-q768643a6ae\">Two perpendicular legs and the displacement arrow.</desc><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"352\" y2=\"206.0\" stroke=\"#999\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#999\"/><text x=\"338\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12\">x</text><text x=\"40.0\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"12\">y</text><defs><marker id=\"arrow-b-q768643a6ae\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L9,4.5 L0,9 z\" fill=\"#2c4fb8\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"163.0\" y2=\"206.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-q768643a6ae)\"/><text x=\"102.5\" y=\"202.0\" font-size=\"12\">30 m E</text><line x1=\"163.0\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"163.0\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-q768643a6ae)\"/><text x=\"167.0\" y=\"116.0\" font-size=\"12\">40 m N</text><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"163.0\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-q768643a6ae)\"/><text x=\"102.5\" y=\"116.0\" font-size=\"12\">50 m</text></svg><figcaption>Walk east then north</figcaption></figure>",
      "source_identity": null,
      "learner_location": "pages/position-and-displacement-in-a-plane.html#q768643a6ae"
    },
    {
      "id": "qe316ae6be0",
      "text": "The position of a particle is x = 3t m and y = 4t m, with t in seconds. Find the speed of the particle.",
      "owner_label": null,
      "authored": false,
      "subtopic": "Velocity and acceleration as vectors",
      "hint": "Read off vₓ and v_y from how x and y change each second.",
      "steps": [
        "x grows by 3 m every second, so vₓ = 3 m/s; y grows by 4 m every second, so v_y = 4 m/s.",
        "Speed = √(3² + 4²) = 5 m/s."
      ],
      "answer": "5 m/s",
      "visual": "<figure data-role=\"visual\"><svg role=\"img\" viewBox=\"0 0 360 240\" aria-labelledby=\"t-b-qe316ae6be0 d-b-qe316ae6be0\"><title id=\"t-b-qe316ae6be0\">Velocity components</title><desc id=\"d-b-qe316ae6be0\">Velocity vector with components 3 and 4 m/s.</desc><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"352\" y2=\"206.0\" stroke=\"#999\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#999\"/><text x=\"338\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12\">x</text><text x=\"40.0\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"12\">y</text><defs><marker id=\"arrow-b-qe316ae6be0\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L9,4.5 L0,9 z\" fill=\"#2c4fb8\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"163.0\" y2=\"206.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-qe316ae6be0)\"/><text x=\"102.5\" y=\"202.0\" font-size=\"12\">3</text><line x1=\"163.0\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"163.0\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-qe316ae6be0)\"/><text x=\"167.0\" y=\"116.0\" font-size=\"12\">4</text><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"163.0\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-qe316ae6be0)\"/><text x=\"102.5\" y=\"116.0\" font-size=\"12\">v</text></svg><figcaption>Velocity components</figcaption></figure>",
      "source_identity": null,
      "learner_location": "pages/velocity-and-acceleration-as-vectors.html#qe316ae6be0"
    },
    {
      "id": "q7a05a97042",
      "text": "A particle's velocity changes from 4 m/s along x to 3 m/s along y in 2 s. Find the magnitude of the average acceleration.",
      "owner_label": null,
      "authored": false,
      "subtopic": "Velocity and acceleration as vectors",
      "hint": "Subtract the velocity vectors, not the speeds.",
      "steps": [
        "Δv = (0 − 4, 3 − 0) = (−4, 3) m/s, so |Δv| = 5 m/s.",
        "Average acceleration = 5 / 2 = 2.5 m/s²."
      ],
      "answer": "2.5 m/s²",
      "visual": "<figure data-role=\"visual\"><svg role=\"img\" viewBox=\"0 0 360 240\" aria-labelledby=\"t-b-q7a05a97042 d-b-q7a05a97042\"><title id=\"t-b-q7a05a97042\">Velocity change</title><desc id=\"d-b-q7a05a97042\">Initial and final velocities and the change between them.</desc><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"352\" y2=\"206.0\" stroke=\"#999\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"8\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#999\"/><text x=\"338\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12\">x</text><text x=\"40.0\" y=\"18\" font-size=\"12\">y</text><defs><marker id=\"arrow-b-q7a05a97042\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" markerWidth=\"9\" markerHeight=\"9\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"4.5\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L9,4.5 L0,9 z\" fill=\"#2c4fb8\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"263.3\" y2=\"206.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-q7a05a97042)\"/><text x=\"152.7\" y=\"202.0\" font-size=\"12\">v₁</text><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-q7a05a97042)\"/><text x=\"38.0\" y=\"116.0\" font-size=\"12\">v₂</text><line x1=\"263.3\" y1=\"206.0\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"34.0\" stroke=\"#2c4fb8\" stroke-width=\"2\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-b-q7a05a97042)\"/><text x=\"152.7\" y=\"116.0\" font-size=\"12\">Δv</text></svg><figcaption>Velocity change</figcaption></figure>",
      "source_identity": null,
      "learner_location": "pages/velocity-and-acceleration-as-vectors.html#q7a05a97042"
    },
    {
      "id": "qf37aead9ab",
      "text": "Two balls are 20 m above the ground. Ball A is dropped and ball B is thrown horizontally at 5 m/s at the same instant. Which reaches the ground first, and when? Take g = 10 m/s².",
      "owner_label": null,
      "authored": false,
      "subtopic": "Perpendicular components are independent",
      "hint": "Compare only the vertical motions.",
      "steps": [
        "Both start with zero vertical velocity and fall 20 m: 20 = ½ × 10 × t².",
        "t² = 4, so t = 2 s for both; they land together."
      ],
      "answer": "They land together after 2 s.",
